## 2. Resulting vertical diffusivity

The CATKE model produces seasonally varying mixing, including short-lived events.

WORKSHOP_NUMERICALEARTH_DIFFUSIVITY_FIGURE

## 3. Smooth idealised forcing

The classroom uses a smooth seasonal approximation so changes in production and
export can be related to biological processes without following individual
weather events. The prescribed mixing depth varies through the year, with strong
mixing above it and weaker mixing below. Both stations use the upper 300 m of the
water column in these plots.

